<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Status-bar icon for pushed alerts.

  Android 5+ discards colour in a notification's small icon and renders only the
  alpha channel, tinting the result. Handing it the launcher icon (which is what
  happens when no default is declared) therefore produces a solid white blob, so
  this is drawn as a white-on-transparent silhouette from the start. The accent
  colour beside it in the manifest is what actually tints it.
-->
